      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-w/q1-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The handwritten small-angle step is sin(−h/2) = −h/2 + O(h3); dividing by h gives −1/2 + O(h2). The limits of the factors are sin x/ cos2 x and 1. Equivalently, using the expanded cosine above, as h →0 in radians, (1 −cos h)/h →0 from the quadratic approximation, and sin h/h →1. [M1] [A1] The limit is sin x/ cos2 x = sec x tan x . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 1 is 7 marks.</p>"
    ],
