    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-w/q14-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The curve C has equation x + 1 x + 1 y = 4 8 × − 2 . Show that an equation of the tangent to the curve, at the point where C crosses the x axis is given by y = ( x + 2 ln2 ) . ( ) 7\" style=\"--madas-width:589.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-w/q14-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"The direct method differentiates to give y′ = 4 · 8x+1 ln 8 −2x+1 ln 2. At a zero, 32 · 8x = 2 · 2x, so 4x = 1/16 = 4−2 . Then the gradient is (1/2) ln 8 −(1/2) ln 2 = (1/2) ln 4 . = ln 2 Equivalently, set u = 2x+1. [M1] [A1] Then 4 · 8x+1 = 4u3, [A1] so the zero of 4u3 −u, with u &gt; 0, is u = 1/2, [A1] or x = −2. [A1] Since u′ = u ln 2, the gradient there is (12u2 −1)u ln 2 = ln 2. [A1] Through (−2, 0) this gives y = (x + 2) ln 2 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
